<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 3 Best in Slot Gear list for Holy Paladin Healer in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Trial of the Grand Crusader. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Holy Paladin Healer Phase 3</h2>
<i>Healer gearing always heavily depends on playstyle, situation and raid environment so treat the BiS list below as a guideline rather than a gospel.</i>
<br/>
<br/>Due to being able to wear all 4 armor types, Holy Paladin gearing can be somewhat overwhelming as it has a ton of options. With a little bit of work and stat evaluations, we can cut this down tremendously and also consider loot priority carefully, as mail and plate spellpower gear is very uncontested in return.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="phase-3-holy-paladin-builds">Phase 3 Holy Paladin Builds</h3>Similar to Phase 2, the T8 4pc bonus is strong enough that you will need several upgrades to replace it, if you even want to. Despite the major stat upgrade of T9 items, T8 4pc continues to be the strongest setup for tank healing, particularly on Anub'arak when maintaining Sacred Shields on tanks. Adding to this, the T9 set bonus for Holy Paladins is so weak that you can fully disregard it entirely and judge it on stats alone. <br/>
<br/>In general, this means an optimized T8 4pc build is your best overall set, particularly for tank-healing focused fights like Anub'arak, to facilitate the highest possible tank effective health pool. However, when tank survival is not your strict focus, you can drop the T8 set bonus for a mostly pure ilvl set with either of these conditions:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">At least two 245 or higher upgrades in legs and helm</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Any 258 legs</div></li></ul>Keep in mind the slots still need to be well itemized; crit/<wbr/>haste is generally most preferred, but haste/<wbr/>mp5 is acceptable. Crit/<wbr/>mp5 items of these ilvls are mediocre despite their higher item level and should not be used, as well as any items with the wasted secondary of spirit.<br/>
<br/>
